WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.510
Crypto-safe C++ starts with the security goal.

2
00:00:03.510 --> 00:00:11.409
Decide whether the system needs confidentiality, integrity, authenticity, identity verification, or another trust decision before choosing an API.

3
00:00:11.409 --> 00:00:14.480
Use trusted libraries and approved platform mechanisms.

4
00:00:14.480 --> 00:00:22.818
Do not implement cryptographic primitives from scratch, and avoid custom protocols when a mature library provides the needed behavior.

5
00:00:22.818 --> 00:00:25.012
Protect keys, randomness, and nonces.

6
00:00:25.012 --> 00:00:33.349
Generate security-sensitive values through approved sources, keep key ownership clear, avoid accidental exposure, and document rotation or lifecycle

7
00:00:33.349 --> 00:00:33.788
policy.

8
00:00:33.788 --> 00:00:41.686
Use authenticated encryption for protected data where appropriate, validate signatures and certificates correctly, and reject data that fails

9
00:00:41.686 --> 00:00:44.758
verification before the application acts on it.

10
00:00:44.758 --> 00:00:47.829
Keep crypto code small, boring, and reviewable.

11
00:00:47.829 --> 00:00:56.166
Treat ignored errors, nonce reuse, hardcoded secrets, custom trust decisions, stale dependencies, and unauthenticated protected data as high-priority

12
00:00:56.166 --> 00:00:56.605
findings.

13
00:00:56.605 --> 00:01:01.871
Finally, combine design review, focused tests, dependency maintenance, and operational key management.

14
00:01:01.871 --> 00:01:07.575
Cryptography works best when the surrounding engineering is disciplined enough to support it.

15
00:01:07.575 --> 00:01:17.229
The durable habit is to make every crypto boundary explainable: goal, API, key source, trust decision, validation result, and safe failure behavior.

16
00:01:17.229 --> 00:01:24.250
When those details are visible, crypto becomes a dependable engineering control instead of a fragile assumption.

17
00:01:24.250 --> 00:01:27.321
That visibility is the habit to keep.

18
00:01:27.321 --> 00:01:27.760
Always.
